There is a concurrency problem in APIs that is easy to miss. Two clients read the same resource: Client A -> GET /documents/42 Client B -> GET /documents/42
Both receive the same version. Client A changes the title and saves it. Then Client B, still working with the older representation, sends another update. Without a concurrency check, the second request can overwrite the first one without knowing that the resource changed in the meantime. This is the classic lost update problem. Doctrine supports optimistic locking with a version field: use Doctrine\ORM\Mapping as ORM;
#[ORM\Entity] class Document { #[ORM\Id] #[ORM\GeneratedValue] #[ORM\Column] private ?int $id = null;
#[ORM\Column(length: 180)] private string $title;
